  "_comment": "The authored half of an archetype: display metadata, the inherent blurb, the five hand-curated scalars, and the primary/secondary roster. NOT here, and deliberately: the binary-derived stats (HP and cap curves, threat, damage cap, the movement and attribute ceilings). Those come from classes.bin via convert-archetypes.cjs and are merged in by convert-archetype-registry.cjs on every regen, so they cannot go stale here. The roster IS authored and is not reproducible from the powerset tree: Homecoming orders its lists for display rather than alphabetically, and the Kheldian/VEAT sets sit under epic/ where a primary/secondary directory walk finds nothing. archetypeOrder is the registry order and is its own field because the two id lists do not imply it: Thunderspy counts primalist among the standard archetypes but places it last in the registry. Archetype ids are sorted so a diff stays readable; field order inside an archetype is authored, and branches depends on it.",
